1
00:00:00,099 --> 00:00:01,740
Those bumpy tiles at the edge of a train

2
00:00:01,779 --> 00:00:03,720
platform are a language, and it only has two

3
00:00:03,819 --> 00:00:04,419
words.

4
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:06,799
Round domes mean stop, because there is an

5
00:00:06,899 --> 00:00:08,819
edge, a road, or a drop ahead.

6
00:00:09,179 --> 00:00:11,159
Long parallel bars mean keep going,

7
00:00:11,319 --> 00:00:12,059
this way is safe.

8
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:14,340
Both are readable through a shoe or the tip

9
00:00:14,359 --> 00:00:16,000
of a cane, and the yellow helps if you

10
00:00:16,039 --> 00:00:16,859
still have some sight.

11
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,039
An engineer in Japan named Seiichi Miyake paid

12
00:00:20,079 --> 00:00:22,219
for the first ones himself in 1965,

13
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:23,739
because a friend was going blind.

14
00:00:24,039 --> 00:00:25,579
They are under most of the world's feet now.
